  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The De Broglie wavelength is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi>mv</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>The momentum is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></math></p><p>The momentum of proton is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></math></p><p>The momentum of electron is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;is the Planck&#39;s constant and it is given that both wavelengths are same, i.e.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>,&nbsp;so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>.</p></blockquote>",
